   <!--
      Test Case: Form 8283 - Noncash Charitable Contributions (Vehicle Donation)

      IRC Section 170 - Charitable Contributions

      Rules Tested:
      - Vehicle donations > $500 require Form 8283
      - Donations > $5,000 require qualified appraisal (IRC §170(f)(11)(C))
      - Deduction generally limited to gross proceeds from sale by charity
      - Special rules if charity uses vehicle for significant exempt use
      - Appraisal must be by qualified appraiser within 60 days of donation
      - Form 1098-C required from donee organization

      Test Scenario:
      - Married couple donates used car to charitable organization
      - Vehicle FMV: $8,000 (Blue Book value)
      - Charity sells vehicle for $7,500 (actual proceeds)
      - Qualified appraisal obtained: $8,000 FMV
      - Donation date: 6/15/2025
      - Appraisal date: 7/10/2025 (within 60 days)
      - Form 1098-C received showing sale proceeds of $7,500

      Expected Results:
      - Charitable deduction: $7,500 (limited to actual sale proceeds)
      - Form 8283 required (donation > $5,000)
      - Appraisal required and obtained
      - Deduction reported on Schedule A
   -->

